title: HTML report
section: Reports
desc: A tour of the self-contained HTML report: overview, results, timeline, dependency graph and history.
lede: One file, no server, works offline. Send it by email or attach it to a CI run.
---
<h2>Create it</h2>
<cb lang="bash">$ npx bddr -f html:reports/report.html
$ open reports/report.html           # macOS
$ start reports\report.html          # Windows</cb>
<figure class="shot"><img src="../assets/img/report-overview.png" alt="The Overview tab of the HTML report: KPI cards, failures grouped by cause, scenario results donut, step bar, duration histogram and slowest scenarios." width="1462" height="936" loading="lazy"></figure>

<h2>What is in it</h2>
<h3>Overview</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Cards for pass rate (with the change from the previous run), duration, parallelism and stability.</li>
  <li>A status chart, duration percentiles and a histogram.</li>
  <li>Failures grouped by cause, the slowest scenarios, and a breakdown by feature, tag and group.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Results</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Every scenario with its steps, errors, logs, screenshots and attachments, and every attempt of a retried scenario.</li>
  <li>Data-driven scenarios (Examples, CSV, Excel, JSON) as one colour-coded table, with a row per scenario and a column per parameter.</li>
  <li>Step tables and doc strings as tables tinted by the status of the step.</li>
  <li>Filters by status, log level, tag and search text.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Execution</h3>
<ul>
  <li>The <strong>timeline</strong>: one lane per worker with a bar for each scenario attempt. Retried attempts are hatched. Worker start-up and busy percentage are shown. There is one row per group. Click a bar to open the scenario.</li>
  <li>The <strong>dependency graph</strong>: scenarios and groups that wait for each other, left to right. Soft dependencies are dashed.</li>
</ul>
<figure class="placeholder" data-kind="screenshot" style="--ratio: 16 / 9">
  <div class="placeholder-frame"><p class="placeholder-what">The Execution tab: the worker timeline and the dependency graph.</p></div>
